markdown <<MARKDOWN
# The Project from Start to Finish

Your students build the same four things in the same order, whatever two categories they pick. Knowing the order lets you tell where a stuck student actually is, and what they need next.

<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 260px; background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px;">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 6px;">
      <div style="width: 32px; height: 32px; min-width: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; line-height: 32px;">1</div>
      <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">Pick two categories</div>
    </div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Your students choose two kinds of images an AI could tell apart, like oceans and rivers, or roses and peonies.</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 8px; color: #1F1976;"><b>Builds on:</b> classification, Lessons 8 and 9</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 260px; background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px;">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 6px;">
      <div style="width: 32px; height: 32px; min-width: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; line-height: 32px;">2</div>
      <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">Turn questions into features</div>
    </div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">They write yes/no questions about the images, like "Are there white waves in the water?" Each good question becomes a feature.</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 8px; color: #1F1976;"><b>Builds on:</b> features, Lessons 8 and 10</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 260px; background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px;">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 6px;">
      <div style="width: 32px; height: 32px; min-width: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; line-height: 32px;">3</div>
      <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">Label the data</div>
    </div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">For each image, they record its category and a yes or no for each of three features, then mark it as training or test data.</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 8px; color: #1F1976;"><b>Builds on:</b> training and test data, Lesson 9</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 260px; background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px;">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 6px;">
      <div style="width: 32px; height: 32px; min-width: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; line-height: 32px;">4</div>
      <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">Build the classifier</div>
    </div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">They turn each row into a Python dictionary, write a distance function that counts how many features two images disagree on, then test and reflect.</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 8px; color: #1F1976;"><b>Builds on:</b> dictionaries, Lesson 10, and nearest neighbors, Lesson 8</div>
  </div>
</div>

## What a Finished Data Table Looks Like

By step 3, each student has a table like this one from the exemplar, with one row per image. Every row becomes one dictionary in step 4.

<div role="table" aria-label="Example labeled data table for oceans and rivers" style="margin: 16px 0; max-width: 700px; border: 1px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden;">
  <div role="row" style="display: flex; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 16px;">
    <div role="columnheader" style="flex: 1; padding: 8px 10px;">Image</div>
    <div role="columnheader" style="flex: 1; padding: 8px 10px;">Category</div>
    <div role="columnheader" style="flex: 1; padding: 8px 10px;">White waves</div>
